# blocked-on-anchor — the decision table (family contract in fixture.yaml; per-row intent below).
# id     | world | patch | env | expect
# line1  = the marker is the ruling's first line — both readers hold (the shape they always agreed on)
# mid    = the marker sits on line 3 under a heading — THE FIXED ROW: the predicate missed it on
#          base (dispatched #240) while the belt kept #241's label; both hold after the fix
# absent = no marker — the negative control: the gate dispatches #240, the belt removes #241's label
# quoted = the ruling QUOTES a past marker (`> blocked-on: human`) and names it mid-sentence — the
#          line anchor latches nothing, so both readers treat it as ordinary-path (IL-T26)
line1  | line1 | | | held
mid    | line1 | | | held
absent | line1 | | | ordinary
quoted | line1 | | | ordinary
